<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: for, min, script,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	Write a script that plays a game of minesweeper with a graphical interface.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>When you click run, your script should perform the following tasks:</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell>
			<p>
				<ul>
					<li>Display welcome message to MATLAB's command window. Use <pf>fprintf.</pf></li>
					<li>Using <pf>input</pf>, prompt the user for the grid size and number of mines.</li>
					<li>Based on the user's inputs, create a minefield with the specified number of mines randomly placed on the grid.</li>
					<li>Define any game state variables you plan to use.</li>
					<li>Display a blank game interface using the code you wrote in the previous homework assignment.</li>
					<li>Write a game loop that plays minesweeper according to the rules in this document .</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>As with Tic-Tac-Toe, if a player clicks on a space that is outside the game area, already revealed, or a flagged space, then nothing should happen. A flagged space must first be unflagged before it can be revealed.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>The main job of your game loop is to wait for a player to click in the game area, process the location of the click, and perform the appropriate action.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

<p>
	Examples:
<program>
	<code>
		You can run
		this code
		to see a sample script running Minesweeper. Just download the file, locate the file inside MATLAB, right-click on the file and select "Run."
	</code>
</program>
</p>
</statement>
